1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,460
Case number zero zero eight.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,120
The subject lives where you would not stand.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:09,040
A ledge as wide as a dinner plate.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,880
Nothing below it but air.

5
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:12,160
And there she is,

6
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:12,420
chewing,

7
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:12,880
calm,

8
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,460
like the mountain owes her rent.

9
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,300
The mountain goat.

10
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,840
And before we go further,

11
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,340
a correction for the record.

12
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,460
She is not a goat at all.

13
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,120
She is a goat-antelope,

14
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,520
a cousin of the chamois.

15
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:25,900
The name stuck.

16
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:27,740
The truth is stranger.

17
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,740
Exhibit one.

18
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:30,740
The feet.

19
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,260
Each hoof splits into two toes,

20
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,180
and those toes can spread apart.

21
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:36,120
Underneath,

22
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:36,800
a soft,

23
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:37,660
rubbery pad.

24
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:38,740
Around it,

25
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,900
a hard outer rim.

26
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,860
The rim catches the edge.

27
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,360
The pad grips the rock like a hand.

28
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,920
The Park Service says it plainly.

29
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,720
Climbing where nothing else can follow is her

30
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,460
main defense.

31
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:52,340
Exhibit two.

32
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,540
The ledge.

33
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,760
When it is time to give birth,

34
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:57,660
the mother does not look for a meadow.

35
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,180
She looks for a cliff.

36
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:00,240
A steep,

37
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,020
hidden shelf,

38
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:02,080
late in the spring.

39
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:04,440
The kid weighs about as much as a

40
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,320
newborn baby.

41
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:06,440
Within minutes,

42
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,300
it is standing.

43
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:09,260
First lesson of life,

44
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,420
taught at altitude.

45
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,640
Hold on.

46
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,520
Exhibit three.

47
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:14,620
The sky.

48
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,280
Golden eagles hunt these cliffs.

49
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,060
Their move is simple.

50
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,500
Strike a young goat,

51
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,580
knock it off the ledge,

52
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,140
and let gravity do the rest.

53
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,260
So scientists watched.

54
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,680
For twelve years.

55
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,640
When eagles went after the goats,

56
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,700
they did not win.

57
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:30,940
Not once.

58
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,360
Because every time,

59
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:33,580
the mother stepped in.

60
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,180
She stood over her kid.

61
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,560
She put her horns toward the sky.

62
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:39,440
Exhibit four.

63
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,360
The cat.

64
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,400
The mountain lion.

65
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:45,200
One study calls it the predator probably best

66
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,000
built for hunting mountain goats.

67
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,220
It is patient.

68
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,560
It climbs.

69
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:50,660
It waits.

70
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:53,420
And that is why she keeps climbing.

71
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,360
Higher,

72
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:54,840
steeper,

73
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,320
narrower.

74
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,880
Every meter up is a meter the hunter

75
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:58,680
has to earn.

76
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:00,480
Exhibit five.

77
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,480
The wall.

78
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,440
In the Italian Alps,

79
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,500
there is a dam.

80
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,580
Forty-nine meters of concrete,

81
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,840
close to straight up.

82
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:08,820
And on it,

83
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,840
Alpine ibex.

84
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,460
Mothers and young ones,

85
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,820
walking the face of the wall,

86
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,420
licking salt off the stone.

87
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,520
They are not showing off.

88
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:17,940
They need the minerals.

89
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,180
So they go where the minerals are.

90
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:23,160
Now the hardest exhibit in the file.

91
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,520
The eagle is not what usually kills them.

92
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:28,020
Neither is the cat.

93
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,320
It is winter.

94
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,820
In British Columbia,

95
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:33,660
biologists found that forty to sixty percent of

96
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,420
kids die in their first winter.

97
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,300
Cold.

98
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,320
Hunger.

99
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,080
Snow over the food.

100
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,840
The cliff protects them from the hunters.

101
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,380
Nothing protects them from the season.

102
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,460
They just have to outlast it.

103
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:49,580
Verdict.

104
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,300
She was born on the edge.

105
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,960
She eats on the edge.

106
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:54,200
She raises her young on the edge.

107
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:56,520
And the edge is the safest place she

108
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:56,820
knows.

109
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,580
Maybe that is the part for us.

110
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,380
The place that scares everybody else might be

111
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,180
the very place that keeps you alive.

112
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,380
The climb is not the danger.

113
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,480
The climb is the defense.

114
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,360
Stay up there.

115
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,420
Hold on.

116
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,080
Outlast the winter.

117
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,020
The Cliff File.

118
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:17,180
Produced by Relentless Aaron.

